text: ['All creatures get -1/-1.', 'Anger of the Gods deals 3 damage to each creature. If a creature dealt damage this way would die this turn, exile it instead.', 'As an additional cost to cast this spell, discard a card.\\nDraw two cards.', "As an additional cost to cast this spell, you may reveal a Dragon card from your hand.\\nDraconic Roar deals 3 damage to target creature. If you revealed a Dragon card or controlled a Dragon as you cast this spell, Draconic Roar deals 3 damage to that creature's controller.", 'As an additional cost to cast this spell, you may reveal a Dragon card from your hand.\\nTarget player sacrifices a creature. If you revealed a Dragon card or controlled a Dragon as you cast this spell, you gain 4 life.', 'As long as you control a Dragon, Dragonloft Idol gets +1/+1 and has flying and trample.', 'As long as your life total is greater than or equal to your starting life total, creatures you control get +1/+1.\\nWhenever one or more creatures you control attack, you gain life equal to the number of attacking creatures.', 'At the beginning of combat on your turn, you may have target creature get +2/+0 until end of turn.', 'At the beginning of each end step, if you gained 4 or more life this turn, create a 4/4 white Angel creature token with flying.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, return an instant or sorcery card at random from your graveyard to your hand.\\nWhenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, Charmbreaker Devils gets +4/+0 until end of turn.', 'At the beginning of your upkeep, you may put a charge counter on Aether Vial.\\n{T}: You may put a creature card with mana value equal to the number of charge counters on Aether Vial from your hand onto the battlefield.', 'Attacking creatures get +2/+0 until end of turn.', "Azorius Chancery enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Azorius Chancery enters the battlefield, return a land you control to its owner's hand.\\n{T}: Add {W}{U}.", "Bladewing's Thrall has flying as long as you control a Dragon.\\nWhen a Dragon enters the battlefield, you may return Bladewing's Thrall from your graveyard to the battlefield.", "Bloodghast can't block.\\nBloodghast has haste as long as an opponent has 10 or less life.\\nLandfall — Whenever a land enters the battlefield under your control, you may return Bloodghast from your graveyard to the battlefield.", "Boros Garrison enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Boros Garrison enters the battlefield, return a land you control to its owner's hand.\\n{T}: Add {R}{W}.", "Cast this spell only if you've cast another spell this turn.\\nFlying", "Choose one —\\n• Creatures you control gain lifelink until end of turn.\\n• Draw a card.\\n• Put target attacking or blocking creature on top of its owner's library.", 'Choose one —\\n• Destroy target artifact.\\n• Target creature gets +1/+1 and gains trample until end of turn.\\n• Remove two time counters from target permanent or suspended card.', "Choose two —\\n• Counter target spell.\\n• Return target permanent to its owner's hand.\\n• Tap all creatures your opponents control.\\n• Draw a card.", 'Choose two —\\n• Destroy all artifacts.\\n• Destroy all enchantments.\\n• Destroy all creatures with mana value 3 or less.\\n• Destroy all creatures with mana value 4 or greater.', 'Counter target instant or sorcery spell unless its controller pays {1}.\\nStorm (When you cast this spell, copy it for each spell cast before it this turn. You may choose new targets for the copies.)', 'Counter target spell unless its controller pays {3}.', 'Counter target spell unless its controller pays {X}. Scry 2. (Look at the top two cards of your library, then put any number of them on the bottom of your library and the rest on top in any order.)', "Counter target spell. At the beginning of your next main phase, add an amount of {C} equal to that spell's mana value.", 'Counter target spell. Scry 1. (Look at the top card of your library. You may put that card on the bottom of your library.)', 'Create a 4/4 green Beast creature token.\\nStorm (When you cast this spell, copy it for each spell cast before it this turn.)', 'Creatures you control get +2/+1 until end of turn.\\nRebound (If you cast this spell from your hand, exile it as it resolves. At the beginning of your next upkeep, you may cast this card from exile without paying its mana cost.)', 'Creatures you control have haste.\\nCreatures your opponents control enter the battlefield tapped.', 'Deathtouch (Any amount of damage this deals to a creature is enough to destroy it.)', "Deathtouch\\nUnleash (You may have this creature enter the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it. It can't block as long as it has a +1/+1 counter on it.)", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\nWhen Carven Caryatid enters the battlefield, draw a card.", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\nWhen Jungle Barrier enters the battlefield, draw a card.", "Defender (This creature can't attack.)\\n{T}: Prevent the next 1 damage that would be dealt to any target this turn.", 'Defender, flying\\nPrevent all combat damage that would be dealt to and dealt by Fog Bank.', 'Defender\\nLandfall — Whenever a land enters the battlefield under your control, you gain 1 life.', 'Defender\\nPut a -0/-1 counter on Wall of Roots: Add {G}. Activate only once each turn.', 'Defender\\nWhen Dragon Egg dies, create a 2/2 red Dragon creature token with flying and "{R}: This creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn."', 'Defender\\nWhen Mnemonic Wall enters the battlefield, you may return target instant or sorcery card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'Defender\\n{1}{R}, {T}: Vent Sentinel deals damage to target player or planeswalker equal to the number of creatures you control with defender.', 'Defender\\n{2}{U}, {T}: Target player mills X cards, where X is the number of creatures you control with defender.', 'Defender\\n{T}: Add {G} for each creature you control with defender.', 'Destroy target artifact or enchantment.', 'Destroy target artifact or enchantment. Its controller gains 4 life.', 'Destroy target creature with flying. You gain 2 life.', 'Destroy target creature with power 3 or less.', "Destroy target nonartifact creature. Its controller mills cards equal to that creature's power.", 'Destroy target nonblack creature.', "Dimir Aqueduct enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Dimir Aqueduct enters the battlefield, return a land you control to its owner's hand.\\n{T}: Add {U}{B}.", 'Double strike\\nSavageborn Hydra enters the battlefield with X +1/+1 counters on it.\\n{1}{R/G}: Put a +1/+1 counter on Savageborn Hydra. Activate only as a sorcery.', 'Dragon creatures you control get +3/+3.', 'Dragon spells you cast cost {1} less to cast.', 'Draw a card for each creature you control with a +1/+1 counter on it. Those creatures gain indestructible until end of turn. (Damage and effects that say "destroy" don\'t destroy them.)', 'Draw three cards, then put a card from your hand on the bottom of your library.', "Each creature you control assigns combat damage equal to its toughness rather than its power.\\n{G}: Target creature with defender can attack this turn as though it didn't have defender.\\n{2}{G}: Creatures you control get +0/+1 until end of turn.", 'Each player discards their hand, then draws cards equal to the greatest number of cards a player discarded this way.', 'Electrolyze deals 2 damage divided as you choose among one or two targets.\\nDraw a card.', 'Enchant creature\\nAll creatures able to block enchanted creature do so.', "Enchant creature\\nAs Pentarch Ward enters the battlefield, choose a color.\\nWhen Pentarch Ward enters the battlefield, draw a card.\\nEnchanted creature has protection from the chosen color. This effect doesn't remove Pentarch Ward.", 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature has defender.', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature has lifelink and "Whenever a creature an opponent controls dies, put a +1/+1 counter on this creature." (Damage dealt by a creature with lifelink also causes its controller to gain that much life.)', "Enchant creature\\nWhen Claustrophobia enters the battlefield, tap enchanted creature.\\nEnchanted creature doesn't untap during its controller's untap step.", "Enchant creature\\nWhen Hammerhand enters the battlefield, target creature can't block this turn.\\nEnchanted creature gets +1/+1 and has haste.", 'Enchant player\\nWhenever a creature attacks enchanted player, put a +1/+1 counter on it.', 'Exile target creature or enchantment.', 'Exile target creature. Its controller gains life equal to its power.', 'First strike\\nSuspend 4—{R} (Rather than cast this card from your hand, you may pay {R} and exile it with four time counters on it. At the beginning of your upkeep, remove a time counter. When the last is removed, you may cast it without paying its mana cost. It has haste.)', "First strike\\nUnleash (You may have this creature enter the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it. It can't block as long as it has a +1/+1 counter on it.)", 'Flash (You may cast this spell any time you could cast an instant.)\\nWhenever Illusory Ambusher is dealt damage, draw that many cards.', "Flash\\nAt the beginning of your end step, draw seven cards.\\nEach opponent's maximum hand size is reduced by seven.", "Flash\\nCreature cards you own that aren't on the battlefield have flash.\\nEach opponent can cast spells only any time they could cast a sorcery.", 'Flash\\nFlying\\nWhen Bogardan Hellkite enters the battlefield, it deals 5 damage divided as you choose among any number of targets.', 'Flash\\nFlying\\nWhen Restoration Angel enters the battlefield, you may exile target non-Angel creature you control, then return that card to the battlefield under your control.', 'Flying', "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\nRenown 1 (When this creature deals combat damage to a player, if it isn't renowned, put a +1/+1 counter on it and it becomes renowned.)", 'Flying, first strike\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, if Firemane Angel is in your graveyard or on the battlefield, you may gain 1 life.\\n{6}{R}{R}{W}{W}: Return Firemane Angel from your graveyard to the battlefield. Activate only during your upkeep.', 'Flying, haste\\nYou may cast sorcery spells as though they had flash. (You may cast them any time you could cast an instant.)', "Flying, trample\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, sacrifice a creature other than Lord of the Pit. If you can't, Lord of the Pit deals 7 damage to you.", "Flying, trample\\nShroud (This creature can't be the target of spells or abilities.)", "Flying, trample\\nYou can't win the game and your opponents can't lose the game.", 'Flying, vigilance', 'Flying, vigilance, indestructible\\nOther permanents you control have indestructible.', 'Flying\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, draw a card unless target opponent sacrifices a creature or pays 3 life.', 'Flying\\nHaste (This creature can attack and {T} as soon as it comes under your control.)\\nWhen Thundermaw Hellkite enters the battlefield, it deals 1 damage to each creature with flying your opponents control. Tap those creatures.', "Flying\\nJace's Phantasm gets +4/+4 as long as an opponent has ten or more cards in their graveyard.", 'Flying\\nLandfall — Whenever a land enters the battlefield under your control, you may create a 1/1 white Bird creature token with flying.', 'Flying\\nLifelink (Damage dealt by this creature also causes you to gain that much life.)\\nWhenever you gain life, put a +1/+1 counter on each creature you control.', 'Flying\\nProwess (Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, this creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.)', "Flying\\nUnleash (You may have this creature enter the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it. It can't block as long as it has a +1/+1 counter on it.)", 'Flying\\nWhen Angel of Mercy enters the battlefield, you gain 3 life.', 'Flying\\nWhen Balustrade Spy enters the battlefield, target player reveals cards from the top of their library until they reveal a land card, then puts those cards into their graveyard.', 'Flying\\nWhen Bladewing the Risen enters the battlefield, you may return target Dragon permanent card from your graveyard to the battlefield.\\n{B}{R}: Dragon creatures get +1/+1 until end of turn.', "Flying\\nWhen Hoarding Dragon enters the battlefield, you may search your library for an artifact card, exile it, then shuffle.\\nWhen Hoarding Dragon dies, you may put the exiled card into its owner's hand.", 'Flying\\nWhen Jugan, the Rising Star dies, you may distribute five +1/+1 counters among any number of target creatures.', 'Flying\\nWhen Keiga, the Tide Star dies, gain control of target creature.', 'Flying\\nWhen Kokusho, the Evening Star dies, each opponent loses 5 life. You gain life equal to the life lost this way.', 'Flying\\nWhen Malfegor enters the battlefield, discard your hand. Each opponent sacrifices a creature for each card discarded this way.', 'Flying\\nWhen Noxious Dragon dies, you may destroy target creature with mana value 3 or less.', 'Flying\\nWhen Rune-Scarred Demon enters the battlefield, search your library for a card, put it into your hand, then shuffle.', 'Flying\\nWhen Ryusei, the Falling Star dies, it deals 5 damage to each creature without flying.', 'Flying\\nWhen Sandstone Oracle enters the battlefield, choose an opponent. If that player has more cards in hand than you, draw cards equal to the difference.', 'Flying\\nWhen Sphinx of Uthuun enters the battlefield, reveal the top five cards of your library. An opponent separates those cards into two piles. Put one pile into your hand and the other into your graveyard.', 'Flying\\nWhen Yosei, the Morning Star dies, target player skips their next untap step. Tap up to five target permanents that player controls.', "Flying\\nWhenever Blizzard Specter deals combat damage to a player, choose one —\\n• That player returns a permanent they control to its owner's hand.\\n• That player discards a card.", 'Flying\\nWhenever Scourge of Valkas or another Dragon enters the battlefield under your control, it deals X damage to any target, where X is the number of Dragons you control.\\n{R}: Scourge of Valkas gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', 'Flying\\nWhenever Shriekgeist deals combat damage to a player, that player mills two cards.', 'Flying\\nWhenever Sustainer of the Realm blocks, it gets +0/+2 until end of turn.', 'Flying\\nWhenever an opponent draws a card, you may draw two cards.', 'Flying\\n{R}: Furnace Whelp gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', 'Gain control of target creature until end of turn. Put a +1/+1 counter on it and untap it. That creature gains haste until end of turn. (It can attack and {T} this turn.)', "Golgari Rot Farm enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Golgari Rot Farm enters the battlefield, return a land you control to its owner's hand.\\n{T}: Add {B}{G}.", "Gruul Turf enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Gruul Turf enters the battlefield, return a land you control to its owner's hand.\\n{T}: Add {R}{G}.", 'Guardian Idol enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add {C}.\\n{2}: Guardian Idol becomes a 2/2 Golem artifact creature until end of turn.', 'Haste\\nProwess (Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, this creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.)', "Haste\\n{T}: Create a token that's a copy of target nonlegendary creature you control, except it has haste. Sacrifice it at the beginning of the next end step.", 'Heat Ray deals X damage to target creature.', "Heroes' Bane enters the battlefield with four +1/+1 counters on it.\\n{2}{G}{G}: Put X +1/+1 counters on Heroes' Bane, where X is its power.", 'If one or more +1/+1 counters would be put on a creature you control, twice that many +1/+1 counters are put on it instead.', 'Indestructible (Effects that say "destroy" don\'t destroy this artifact.)\\nEquipped creature gets +2/+0.\\nEquip {2}', 'Ivy Elemental enters the battlefield with X +1/+1 counters on it.', "Izzet Boilerworks enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Izzet Boilerworks enters the battlefield, return a land you control to its owner's hand.\\n{T}: Add {U}{R}.", 'Knight of the Reliquary gets +1/+1 for each land card in your graveyard.\\n{T}, Sacrifice a Forest or Plains: Search your library for a land card, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', 'Landfall — Whenever a land enters the battlefield under your control, add one mana of any color.', 'Landfall — Whenever a land enters the battlefield under your control, you may have target player lose 3 life. If you do, put three +1/+1 counters on Ob Nixilis, the Fallen.', 'Lifelink', 'Lifelink (Damage dealt by this creature also causes you to gain that much life.)\\nAs long as you have 30 or more life, Serra Ascendant gets +5/+5 and has flying.', 'Lifelink, protection from white and from black\\nAs long as you have 30 or more life and an opponent has 10 or less life, Blood Baron of Vizkopa gets +6/+6 and has flying.', 'Lightning Helix deals 3 damage to any target and you gain 3 life.', 'Look at the top five cards of your library. You may reveal any number of creature cards from among them and put the revealed cards into your hand. Put the rest on the bottom of your library in any order.', 'Nonbasic lands are Mountains.', "Orzhov Basilica enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Orzhov Basilica enters the battlefield, return a land you control to its owner's hand.\\n{T}: Add {W}{B}.", 'Outlast {1}{W} ({1}{W}, {T}: Put a +1/+1 counter on this creature. Outlast only as a sorcery.)\\nEach creature you control with a +1/+1 counter on it has first strike.', 'Outlast {B} ({B}, {T}: Put a +1/+1 counter on this creature. Outlast only as a sorcery.)\\nEach creature you control with a +1/+1 counter on it has deathtouch.', 'Outlast {W} ({W}, {T}: Put a +1/+1 counter on this creature. Outlast only as a sorcery.)\\nEach creature you control with a +1/+1 counter on it has flying.', 'Outlast {W} ({W}, {T}: Put a +1/+1 counter on this creature. Outlast only as a sorcery.)\\nEach creature you control with a +1/+1 counter on it has lifelink.', 'Phantom Tiger enters the battlefield with two +1/+1 counters on it.\\nIf damage would be dealt to Phantom Tiger, prevent that damage. Remove a +1/+1 counter from Phantom Tiger.', 'Pillar of Flame deals 2 damage to any target. If a creature dealt damage this way would die this turn, exile it instead.', 'Protection from black and from red\\nWhenever another creature enters the battlefield, you may gain 1 life.', 'Protection from red\\nSacrifice Burrenton Forge-Tender: Prevent all damage a red source of your choice would deal this turn.', 'Prowess (Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, this creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.)\\nWhenever Jhessian Thief deals combat damage to a player, draw a card.', 'Prowess (Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, this creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.)\\nWhenever you cast a noncreature spell, Seeker of the Way gains lifelink until end of turn.', "Put a +1/+1 counter on target creature you control. Then that creature fights target creature you don't control. (Each deals damage equal to its power to the other.)", "Rakdos Carnarium enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Rakdos Carnarium enters the battlefield, return a land you control to its owner's hand.\\n{T}: Add {B}{R}.", 'Reach (This creature can block creatures with flying.)\\nWhenever Netcaster Spider blocks a creature with flying, Netcaster Spider gets +2/+0 until end of turn.', "Renown 1 (When this creature deals combat damage to a player, if it isn't renowned, put a +1/+1 counter on it and it becomes renowned.)\\n{2}{G}: Regenerate Undercity Troll. (The next time this creature would be destroyed this turn, it isn't. Instead tap it, remove all damage from it, and remove it from combat.)", "Return all attacking creatures to their owner's hand.", 'Return an instant card at random from your graveyard to your hand.\\nRebound (If you cast this spell from your hand, exile it as it resolves. At the beginning of your next upkeep, you may cast this card from exile without paying its mana cost.)', "Return target nonland permanent with mana value X to its owner's hand.\\nDraw a card.", "Reveal the top X cards of your library. You may put any number of permanent cards with mana value X or less from among them onto the battlefield. Then put all cards revealed this way that weren't put onto the battlefield into your graveyard.", 'Rift Bolt deals 3 damage to any target.\\nSuspend 1—{R} (Rather than cast this card from your hand, you may pay {R} and exile it with a time counter on it. At the beginning of your upkeep, remove a time counter. When the last is removed, you may cast it without paying its mana cost.)', 'Sacrifice Moonglove Extract: It deals 2 damage to any target.', 'Search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield, then shuffle.\\nSuspend 2—{G} (Rather than cast this card from your hand, you may pay {G} and exile it with two time counters on it. At the beginning of your upkeep, remove a time counter. When the last is removed, you may cast it without paying its mana cost.)', "Selesnya Sanctuary enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Selesnya Sanctuary enters the battlefield, return a land you control to its owner's hand.\\n{T}: Add {G}{W}.", "Simic Growth Chamber enters the battlefield tapped.\\nWhen Simic Growth Chamber enters the battlefield, return a land you control to its owner's hand.\\n{T}: Add {G}{U}.", 'Skip your draw step.\\nWhenever you discard a card, exile that card from your graveyard.\\nPay 1 life: Exile the top card of your library face down. Put that card into your hand at the beginning of your next end step.', 'Staggershock deals 2 damage to any target.\\nRebound (If you cast this spell from your hand, exile it as it resolves. At the beginning of your next upkeep, you may cast this card from exile without paying its mana cost.)', 'Star Compass enters the battlefield tapped.\\n{T}: Add one mana of any color that a basic land you control could produce.', 'Suspend 4—{U} (Rather than cast this card from your hand, pay {U} and exile it with four time counters on it. At the beginning of your upkeep, remove a time counter. When the last is removed, you may cast it without paying its mana cost.)\\nTarget player draws three cards.', 'Suspend 5—{G} (Rather than cast this card from your hand, you may pay {G} and exile it with five time counters on it. At the beginning of your upkeep, remove a time counter. When the last is removed, you may cast it without paying its mana cost. It has haste.)', "Swampwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Swamp.)\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, return target creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield.\\nAt the beginning of each opponent's upkeep, that player sacrifices a creature.", "Tap target creature. It doesn't untap during its controller's next untap step.\\nRebound (If you cast this spell from your hand, exile it as it resolves. At the beginning of your next upkeep, you may cast this card from exile without paying its mana cost.)", 'Target creature gets +1/+0 and gains first strike until end of turn.\\nDraw a card.', "Target creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn and can't be blocked this turn.\\nRebound (If you cast this spell from your hand, exile it as it resolves. At the beginning of your next upkeep, you may cast this card from exile without paying its mana cost.)", 'Target creature gets +2/+0 and gains deathtouch until end of turn.\\nRebound (If you cast this spell from your hand, exile it as it resolves. At the beginning of your next upkeep, you may cast this card from exile without paying its mana cost.)', 'Target creature gets +2/+2 and gains trample until end of turn.\\nDraw a card.', 'Target creature gets +2/+2 until end of turn.\\nRebound (If you cast this spell from your hand, exile it as it resolves. At the beginning of your next upkeep, you may cast this card from exile without paying its mana cost.)', 'Target creature gets +3/+0 and gains lifelink until end of turn. Regenerate it. (Damage dealt by a creature with lifelink also causes its controller to gain that much life.)', "Target creature gets +7/+7 and gains trample until end of turn. It must be blocked this turn if able. (A creature with trample can deal excess combat damage to the player or planeswalker it's attacking.)", 'Target creature gets -3/-0 until end of turn.\\nDraw a card.', 'Target creature gets -3/-3 until end of turn. You lose 3 life.', 'Target creature has base power and toughness 1/1 until end of turn.', 'Target creature you control gains protection from the color of your choice until end of turn.\\nRebound (If you cast this spell from your hand, exile it as it resolves. At the beginning of your next upkeep, you may cast this card from exile without paying its mana cost.)', 'Target opponent reveals their hand. You choose a noncreature, nonland card from it. That player discards that card.', 'Target player discards two cards unless they discard an artifact card.', 'Target player discards two cards. If you cast this spell during your main phase, that player discards four cards instead.', 'Target player mills ten cards.', 'Target player mills two cards.\\nDraw a card.', 'Target player reveals their hand. You choose a nonland card from it. That player discards that card. You lose 2 life.', 'Target player sacrifices an attacking creature.\\nStorm (When you cast this spell, copy it for each spell cast before it this turn. You may choose new targets for the copies.)', "This spell can't be countered.\\nDestroy all creatures.", 'This spell costs {1} more to cast for each target beyond the first.\\nFireball deals X damage divided evenly, rounded down, among any number of targets.', "Trample (This creature can deal excess combat damage to the player or planeswalker it's attacking.)", 'Trample\\nEach creature you control with a +1/+1 counter on it has trample.', 'Trample\\nLandfall — Whenever a land enters the battlefield under your control, you may create a 4/4 green Beast creature token.', 'Trample\\nWhenever Primeval Titan enters the battlefield or attacks, you may search your library for up to two land cards, put them onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', "Trample\\nWhenever you tap a land for mana, add one mana of any type that land produced.\\nWhenever an opponent taps a land for mana, that land doesn't untap during its controller's next untap step.", "Unleash (You may have this creature enter the battlefield with a +1/+1 counter on it. It can't block as long as it has a +1/+1 counter on it.)", 'Until end of turn, any time you could activate a mana ability, you may pay 1 life. If you do, add {C}.', 'Up to two target creatures each get +1/+0 and gain first strike until end of turn.', "Vigilance (Attacking doesn't cause this creature to tap.)\\nRenown 1 (When this creature deals combat damage to a player, if it isn't renowned, put a +1/+1 counter on it and it becomes renowned.)", 'Vigilance\\nOther creatures you control get +2/+2.\\nCreatures your opponents control get -2/-2.', 'Vigilance\\nProwess (Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, this creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.)', 'When Bala Ged Scorpion enters the battlefield, you may destroy target creature with power 1 or less.', 'When Chronicler of Heroes enters the battlefield, draw a card if you control a creature with a +1/+1 counter on it.', 'When Day of the Dragons enters the battlefield, exile all creatures you control. Then create that many 5/5 red Dragon creature tokens with flying.\\nWhen Day of the Dragons leaves the battlefield, sacrifice all Dragons you control. Then return the exiled cards to the battlefield under your control.', 'When Doomed Traveler dies, create a 1/1 white Spirit creature token with flying.', 'When Festering Newt dies, target creature an opponent controls gets -1/-1 until end of turn. That creature gets -4/-4 instead if you control a creature named Bogbrew Witch.', "When Frost Lynx enters the battlefield, tap target creature an opponent controls. That creature doesn't untap during its controller's next untap step.", 'When Nantuko Shaman enters the battlefield, if you control no tapped lands, draw a card.\\nSuspend 1—{2}{G}{G} (Rather than cast this card from your hand, you may pay {2}{G}{G} and exile it with a time counter on it. At the beginning of your upkeep, remove a time counter. When the last is removed, you may cast it without paying its mana cost. It has haste.)', 'When Obstinate Baloth enters the battlefield, you gain 4 life.\\nIf a spell or ability an opponent controls causes you to discard Obstinate Baloth, put it onto the battlefield instead of putting it into your graveyard.', 'When Phyrexian Rager enters the battlefield, you draw a card and you lose 1 life.', 'When Radiant Fountain enters the battlefield, you gain 2 life.\\n{T}: Add {C}.', "When Rotfeaster Maggot enters the battlefield, exile target creature card from a graveyard. You gain life equal to that card's toughness.", 'When Runed Servitor dies, each player draws a card.', 'When Timberland Guide enters the battlefield, put a +1/+1 counter on target creature.', 'When you cast this spell, reveal the top X cards of your library. You may put a nonland permanent card with mana value X or less from among them onto the battlefield. Then shuffle the rest into your library.\\nGenesis Hydra enters the battlefield with X +1/+1 counters on it.', 'Whenever Borderland Marauder attacks, it gets +2/+0 until end of turn.', 'Whenever Spiritmonger deals damage to a creature, put a +1/+1 counter on Spiritmonger.\\n{B}: Regenerate Spiritmonger.\\n{G}: Spiritmonger becomes the color of your choice until end of turn.', 'Whenever a creature with flying enters the battlefield under your control, it gains haste until end of turn.\\nWhenever a Dragon enters the battlefield under your control, it deals X damage to any target, where X is the number of Dragons you control.', 'Whenever a creature you control with toughness 4 or greater dies, you gain 4 life.', 'Whenever an opponent loses life, that player mills that many cards. (Damage causes loss of life.)', 'Whenever equipped creature attacks, defending player reveals cards from the top of their library until they reveal a land card. The creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn for each card revealed this way. That player puts the revealed cards into their graveyard.\\nEquip {2}', "Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, Elusive Spellfist gets +1/+0 until end of turn and can't be blocked this turn.", 'Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, you gain 2 life.', 'Whenever you cast a noncreature spell, you may pay {1}{U}. If you do, create a 2/2 blue Djinn Monk creature token with flying.', 'Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, Guttersnipe deals 2 damage to each opponent.', 'Whenever you cast an instant or sorcery spell, Kiln Fiend gets +3/+0 until end of turn.', "Whenever you gain life, put a +1/+1 counter on Ajani's Pridemate.", 'Whenever you gain life, target opponent loses that much life.', "Wight of Precinct Six gets +1/+1 for each creature card in your opponents' graveyards.", 'You gain 2 life. Then if you have more life than an opponent, draw a card.\\nRebound (If you cast this spell from your hand, exile it as it resolves. At the beginning of your next upkeep, you may cast this card from exile without paying its mana cost.)', '{1}, {T}, Sacrifice a creature: You gain 4 life.\\n{1}, {T}, Sacrifice a creature named Festering Newt: Each opponent loses 4 life. You gain life equal to the life lost this way.', '{1}{W}{B}: Target creature gains lifelink until end of turn.\\n{1}{W}{B}: Whenever you gain life this turn, each opponent loses that much life.', '{2}, {T}: Search your library for a card named Festering Newt or Bubbling Cauldron, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', '{4}, {T}: Put a fate counter on target permanent.\\n{5}, {T}, Sacrifice Oblivion Stone: Destroy each nonland permanent without a fate counter on it, then remove all fate counters from all permanents.', '{T}, Pay 1 life: Add {G} or {W}.\\n{1}, {T}, Sacrifice Horizon Canopy: Draw a card.', '{T}, Pay 3 life: Flip a coin. If you win the flip, you gain 6 life.', '{T}, Sacrifice Evolving Wilds: Search your library for a basic land card, put it onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', "{T}, Sacrifice Mishra's Bauble: Look at the top card of target player's library. Draw a card at the beginning of the next turn's upkeep.", '{T}: Add {B} or {R}.\\n{4}{B}{R}: Kolaghan Monument becomes a 4/4 black and red Dragon artifact creature with flying until end of turn.', '{T}: Add {C}.', '{T}: Add {C}. You gain 1 life.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\nAny time you could mulligan and Serum Powder is in your hand, you may exile all the cards from your hand, then draw that many cards. (You can do this in addition to taking mulligans.)', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}, Sacrifice Mind Stone: Draw a card.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{1}, {T}: Add one mana of any color.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{B/R}, {T}: Add {B}{B}, {B}{R}, or {R}{R}.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {R} or {G}. Each opponent gains 1 life.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {W}. Activate only if you control an Island.\\n{T}: Add {U}. Activate only if you control a Plains.', '{T}: Add {C}{C}.', '{T}: Add {C}{C}{C}.', '{T}: Add {C}{C}{C}{C}. Spend this mana only on costs that contain {X}.', '{T}: Add {U}. If you played a land this turn, add {B} instead.', '{T}: Prodigal Pyromancer deals 1 damage to any target.', '{T}: Target attacking creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', '{T}: Target player draws two cards, then discards two cards.', '{W}, {T}: Tap target creature.']
flavor: ['"All peoples treasure a place where the weary traveler may drink in peace."\\n—Ajani Goldmane', '"Any dream is a robust harvest. Still, I prefer the timeworn dreams, heavy with import, that haunt the obsessive mind."', '"Arcum is a babbling fool! Phyrexian technology is our greatest blessing. Take this delightful trinket for instance . . ."\\n—Heidar, Rimewind master', '"As you inject the *viscus vitae* into the brain stem, don\'t let the spastic moaning bother you. It will soon become music to your ears."\\n—Stitcher Geralf', '"Blood is constant. Every drop I drink, someone must bleed."\\n—Vradeen, vampire nocturnus', '"Can you build a fire? Track a deer? Identify killer trees? Then you\'ll never survive Kessig without me."', '"Do you hear that, Sarkhan? The glory of the horde! I made a legend from what you abandoned."\\n—Zurgo, khan of the Mardu', '"Don\'t worry. I\'m not going to deprive you of all your secrets. Just your most precious one."\\n—Liliana Vess', '"Each night, the artificer tucked the little doll into a locked drawer. Each morning, she awoke to find it waiting beside her with some new bauble."\\n—"The Artificer\'s Apprentice"', '"Even this primitive specimen of my kind is impressive."\\n—Niv-Mizzet', '"Hold the line, for family and the fallen!"', '"How can we wage war against ourselves? What happens when the kami of our very souls rise against us? I answer simply: We cannot. We die. There can be no victory in this war."\\n—Sensei Hisoka, letter to Lord Konda', '"Human enlightenment is a firefly that sparks in the night. Dragon enlightenment is a beacon that disperses all darkness."', '"Hunters feed on the fear of their prey."\\n—Garruk Wildspeaker', '"I am confident that if anyone actually penetrates our facades, even the most perceptive would still be fundamentally unprepared for the truth of House Dimir."\\n—Szadek', '"I believe many worlds will bow to Phyrexia. Mirrodin is merely the first."\\n—Sheoldred, Whispering One', '"I carry the light of truth. Do not pity those it blinds, for they never had eyes to see."', '"I don\'t know where my destiny lies, but I know it isn\'t here."', '"I found a new toy. Wanna play?"', '"I knew I\'d find a use for all that newt spittle!"', '"I was not convinced you had a soul until I saw it for myself."\\n—Liliana Vess', '"I was told these were standard issue. Do I look standard to you?"', '"If it were merely lethal, that would be sufficient. The art, however, is in maximizing the suffering it causes."\\n—Liliana Vess', '"In a daze, I woke and looked upon the battlefield, where I could swear my dreams were laying waste to the enemy."\\n—Letter from a soldier', '"It augments anamnesis. What is so confusing about that?"\\n—Perisophia the philosopher', '"It is not a goal, but a process—the process of creating the perfect Phyrexia."', '"Knowledge of Bant\'s landscape and ruins is a weapon that the invaders can\'t comprehend."\\n—Elspeth Tirel', '"Last time, it tore up the Wilt-Leaf, turned Mistmeadow into a mudhole, and made the river jump its banks. On the bright side, we were eating venison for weeks."\\n—Donal Alloway, cenn of Kinscaer', '"Learn to see an obstacle from a new perspective. Underneath, for example."\\n—Chanyi, Ojutai monk', '"Let go of your memories and be reborn."\\n—Argent Etchings, plate 106, passage 27', '"Mana grows and changes like the roots of a plant. Like a plant, it must be nurtured."\\n—Nissa Revane', '"May the Ancestor strengthen my hand and guide my blade."\\n—Nomad war prayer', '"May the worthy spend an eternity in Blessed Sleep. May the wicked find the peace of oblivion."', '"My scars are my sigils. I will wear them with pride long after you\'re gone."', '"My summoning begins your debt, Planeswalker."', '"Now is the hour. Ours is the duty. For victory and family—charge!"', '"Our enemy is nothing less than the end of all life. We shall not want for allies."\\n—*The War Diaries*', '"Rage is not the answer. Rage followed by fitting vengeance is the answer."\\n—Ajani Goldmane', '"Rich" is a relative term.', '"Shame we\'ll never see what all the fuss was about."', '"Swords, to me! We must engage their line to protect our archers and mages. Let no one fail this task!"', '"Teferi snapped his fingers, and the viashino started clucking like a chicken. Silly, yes, but exactly the thing we needed to break the stifling tension."\\n—Jhoira, master artificer', '"The Gitaxians whisper among themselves of other worlds. If they exist, we must bring Phyrexia\'s magnificence to them."', '"The Westfolk wept, and their tears wore winding rivers into the cheek of the world."\\n—Glem the Lonebard, "Origins of Kholon"', '"The dragon is a perfect marriage of power and the will to use it."\\n—Sarkhan Vol', '"The hardest thing is finding the right ingredients."', '"The timeless, tireless jaws of nature shall one day devour us all."\\n—Sildark, artificer of Omu', '"The tools of evil are mere things. And like all things, they cannot last forever."\\n—*Song of All*, canto 881', '"The union of sea and sky makes a perfect cover."\\n—Talrand, sky summoner', '"There was clearly a scream. I\'m not sure if there was a mouth."\\n—Sachir, Akoum Expeditionary House', '"Tools and artisans can be destroyed, but the act of creation is inviolate."\\n—Elspeth Tirel', '"Unwelcome thoughts crowd my mind. Are they my own madness, or the whispers of another?"\\n—Sarkhan Vol', '"Violence is the food it craves. Feed it if you dare."\\n—Doriel, mentor of Mistral Isle', '"Watch people flock to a murder scene. Then tell me we\'re not all a little sick in the head."\\n—Juri, proprietor of the Juri Revue', '"We are a clachan of smiths. The forge is as comfortable to us as a small fire during a cool winter\'s evening."', '"We\'ve bred out the shortcomings of the species\' natural form and replaced them with assets of our own design."\\n—Momir Vig', '"What am I looking at? Ashes, dead man."', '"What is mana but possibility, an idea not yet given form?"\\n—Jhoira, master artificer', '"When one of us prospers, the pride prospers."\\n—Jazal Goldmane', '"When the land is angry, so are they."\\n—Nissa Revane', '"Where\'s the fun in an escape if it\'s not at least a little daring?"', '"Wherever I walk, the ancestors walk too."', '"You can come back once you\'ve learned some manners—and figured out how to reconstitute your physical forms."', '"You can have the body, necromancer. I just want the skin."', '"You thought only the gods could stop you?"', '"Your deed cannot be undone. You, however, can be."\\n—Agosto, Azorius imperator', '"Zendikar fortifies itself against the Great Threat, making sentries of sky, sea, and stone."\\n—*The War Diaries*', 'A demon cannot be trusted, and a dragon will not be ruled.', 'A golden helix streaked skyward from the Helvault. A thunderous explosion shattered the silver monolith and Avacyn emerged, free from her prison at last.', 'A shadow of life chasing a husk of glory.', 'Adepts of the Riverwheel Stronghold can run through rain and never get wet; masters use the raindrops as stepping stones.', "Although the door is flimsy and the lock pathetically small, Josuri's family never fears the night outside.", 'As demons are drawn to suffering, angels are drawn to acts of benevolence.', 'As the bounty on Massacre Girl rose, so did the number of imitators.', 'Atarka serving-goblins coat themselves with grease imbued with noxious herbs, hoping to discourage their ravenous masters from adding them to the meal.', "Baby dragons can't figure out humans—if they didn't want to be killed, why were they made of meat and treasure?", 'Beneath the gaze of angels, only the righteous may stand without fear.', 'Blessed by the hands of Jin-Gitaxias.', 'Bone, stone . . . both taste the same to a hungry basilisk.', 'Cephalids value the free exchange of ideas—except for the "free" part.', 'Diluted, moonglove can etch living tissue. Concentrated, a drop will kill a giant.', 'Dragon birth lairs are littered with treasure to entice the young from their eggs.', "Dragons of Silumgar's brood begin to digest their prey even before consuming it, letting their caustic breath do much of the work.", 'Dragons scorn the weak, even among their own kind.', 'Earth elementals have the eternal strength of stone and the endurance of mountains. Primordially connected to the land they inhabit, they take a long-term view of things, scorning the impetuous haste of short-lived mortal creatures.', 'Enthusiasm is no match for preparation.', 'Even the lost and undead need a protector.', 'Even the wicked have nightmares.', 'Every tear shed is a drop of immortality.', "Everything seems a little less ferocious when it's running from a house cat.", 'Faith in Serra is its own reward.', 'Fast and lethal, with a penchant for the weak and infirm.', 'Follow the light. In its absence, follow her.', 'For Mittens, it was just another day at the beach.', 'For hundreds of years Ugin slept, encased in the cocoon of stone and magic Sarkhan had created using a shard of a Zendikari hedron. As Ugin lay dormant, his spectral guardians kept vigil.', "He has spent years training his eyes and ears to detect the subtle signs of a dragon's approach.", "He vowed he would never rest until he reached his destination. He doesn't know how right he was.", "He's the unlife of the party.", 'Heavier than it looks, tricky to wield, guaranteed to last.', 'His slaves crave death more than they desire freedom. He denies them both.', 'His spark lost, he plots revenge upon the plane whose corrupting mana fractured his soul.', 'In the abstract memories of the Iquati, Jace found interesting ideas to improve upon.', 'In the gardens of the centaurs, many travelers have mysteriously vanished while admiring the elaborate topiaries.', 'In the towering trees of the Samok Stand and the predators that guard them, the might of the Ravnican wild has returned.', 'Is it an amalgamation of faded memories or the projection of a half-remembered dream? Neither answer offers any comfort.', 'Is it at the top of the food chain or the bottom?', "It doesn't point north. It points home.", 'It is an expert at culling individuals who stray too far from the herd.', 'It makes the insignificant conspicuous, the repulsive alluring, and the deadly irresistible.', 'It readily attacks much larger prey, knowing retaliation is impossible.', 'It traps an explosion within its stony skin.', 'It\'s hard to shout "Shields up!" with a javelin in your chest.', "Its back bubbles like a witch's cauldron, and it smells just as vile.", 'Its scales contain the essence of thousands of lotus blooms.', 'Kolaghan has no lasting home, but her disciples leave relics to mark her conquests.', "Leonos had no second thoughts about the abolishment edict. He'd left skyrunes warning of the eviction, even though it was cloudy.", "Mirrodin's deepest caverns conceal its brightest hopes.", "Night after night, Rosheen babbled about a bygone sunlit world, her every word dismissed as a madwoman's ravings.", 'Of royal blood among the spirits of the air, the Mahamoti djinn rides on the wings of the winds. As dangerous in the gambling hall as he is in battle, he is a master of trickery and misdirection.', "Ojutai's words must be translated from Draconic before his students can benefit from their wisdom.", 'On Murasa, even the trees grow trees.', 'One piercing stare usually convinces thieves to go elsewhere.', 'Rakdos cultists are her best customers. They never flinch at pain and are seldom good at math.', "Rakdos rioters paint their faces to resemble the drakes' bloodied muzzles.", 'Scholars had puzzled for centuries over the ruins at Tal Terig. Its secrets had always lived within one rune-carved head.', 'Shamans of Kar-Sengir claim that their sun sets because it can no longer bear the gaze of those pain-carved cliffs.', 'She paints pictures with words, though not all pictures show the truth.', 'Sins that would be too gruesome in the light of day are made more pleasing in the dark of night.', 'So-called "old wood" is rare in deforested Ravnica. Statues carved from it are said to house the last of the ancient nature spirits.', 'Spring is the most beautiful season in the grove, when the new leaves open from their ember-buds in a race of leaping flames.', 'The Crave made Kneecleaver think she was bigger than the dragon.', 'The Izzet learn something from every lesson they teach.', 'The best way to calm a rampaging ceratok is to wait until it dies of natural causes.', 'The calligraphy of combat is written with strokes of sudden blood.', 'The caress of the morning star frees all from the clutch of darkness.', 'The course of the falling star always ends in ruin.', 'The day is born within its branches.', 'The fall of the evening star never heralds a gentle dawn.', 'The fastest way across the dunes is above.', 'The fatal flaw in every plan is the assumption that you know more than your enemy.', 'The flame of anger is hard to douse once lit.', "The hymn's melody has persisted since Tourach's time, but the words changed to invoke the phobias of each listener.", 'The idols were forged during the time of the Khanfall, when the dragons came to rule Tarkir and its people aligned themselves with the five dragonlords.', 'The land is ever resilient. Should it die, it will be reborn.', 'The light of the rising star empowers the champions of tomorrow.', 'The litany of the infernal on his flesh pulses to the beating of his dark heart.', "The mask isn't meant to hide his identity. It's meant to keep the viscera out of his eyes.", 'The myr are like the Glimmervoid: blank canvases on which to build grand creations.', 'The promise of anguish is payment enough for services rendered.', 'The pull of the tide star holds eternal sway.', 'The shaman rattles not to inspire a battle fury but to drown out the shrieks of those fleeing the Eldrazi.', 'The smallest seed of regret can bloom into redemption.', 'The spell fell upon the crowd like a dragon, ancient and full of death.', 'The void is without substance but cuts like steel.', 'There was no reason to pray. This was already an act of the gods.', 'Though she is rightly feared, there are relatively few tales of her deeds in battle, for few survive her raids.', 'Tidal forces of the blood moon wrench and buckle the land, drawing monoliths of stone and soil toward the flaming orb.', "To find its center is to find one's own.", 'To save this plane, he must forsake all others.', 'To some mages, the meaning of life is less important than how much is left.', "Travelers' tales claim that hydras bite off their own heads to make themselves deadlier.", 'Two times the size, four times the smell.', 'Untold riches await those who forsake the bustling world to search the secret, silent places.', "Urza's metathran children were conceived, birthed, and nurtured by an integrated system of machines.", 'Weakness is not in the nature of the Swarm.', 'What is the sound of one head snapping?', 'When nature calls, *run*.', 'When the Mirran resistance arrived, the furnace dwellers looked to Urabrask for guidance. His decree stunned the others: "Let them be."', 'When the earth shudders, the sky overflows.', 'Within silent clearings guarded by living palisades, the natural world guards its most precious secrets.', 'Wounds of the flesh are easy to heal. Wounds of the mind may never be undone.', "You may break her shield, but you'll never break her spirit."]
artist: ['Adam Paquette', 'Adam Rex', 'Adi Granov', 'Alan Pollack', 'Aleksi Briclot', 'Allen Williams', 'Andreas Rocha', 'Anna Steinbauer', 'Anthony Palumbo', 'Anthony S. Waters', 'Ash Wood', 'Austin Hsu', 'BD', 'Brad Rigney', 'Brandon Kitkouski', 'Chippy', 'Chris J. Anderson', 'Chris Rahn', 'Christine Choi', 'Chuck Lukacs', 'Cliff Childs', 'Clint Cearley', 'Craig J Spearing', 'Cynthia Sheppard', 'D. Alexander Gregory', 'Daarken', 'Dan Dos Santos', 'Dan Frazier', 'Dan Murayama Scott', 'Daniel Ljunggren', 'Dany Orizio', 'Daren Bader', 'Dave Dorman', 'Dave Kendall', 'David Palumbo', 'David Rapoza', 'Dominick Domingo', 'Donato Giancola', 'Efrem Palacios', 'Eric Deschamps', 'Erica Yang', 'Filip Burburan', 'Franz Vohwinkel', 'Gabor Szikszai', 'Goran Josic', 'Greg Staples', 'Grzegorz Rutkowski', 'Hideaki Takamura', 'Howard Lyon', 'Igor Kieryluk', 'Izzy', 'Jack Wang', 'Jaime Jones', 'James Paick', 'James Ryman', 'Jana Schirmer & Johannes Voss', 'Jason A. Engle', 'Jason Chan', 'Jason Felix', 'Jason Rainville', 'Jeremy Jarvis', 'Jesper Ejsing', 'Jim Murray', 'Jim Nelson', 'Johann Bodin', 'Johannes Voss', 'John Avon', 'John Severin Brassell', 'John Stanko', 'Jung Park', 'Karl Kopinski', 'Kekai Kotaki', 'Kev Walker', 'Kieran Yanner', 'Lars Grant-West', 'Lius Lasahido', 'Lucas Graciano', 'Mark Zug', 'Mathias Kollros', 'Matt Cavotta', 'Matt Stewart', 'Matt Thompson', 'Matthew D. Wilson', 'Michael C. Hayes', 'Michael Komarck', 'Mike Bierek', 'Miles Johnston', 'Nick Percival', 'Noah Bradley', 'Paolo Parente', 'Pete Venters', 'Peter Mohrbacher', 'Ralph Horsley', 'Randy Gallegos', 'Raoul Vitale', 'Raymond Swanland', 'Rebecca Guay', 'Richard Wright', 'Ron Spears', 'Ron Spencer', 'Ryan Barger', 'Ryan Pancoast', 'Sam Burley', 'Scott Chou', 'Scott M. Fischer', 'Scott Murphy', 'Seb McKinnon', 'Shreya Shetty', 'Slawomir Maniak', 'Stephan Martiniere', 'Steve Argyle', 'Steve Prescott', 'Steven Belledin', 'Svetlin Velinov', 'Terese Nielsen', 'Tomasz Jedruszek', 'Trevor Claxton', 'Tyler Jacobson', 'Viktor Titov', 'Volkan Baǵa', 'Warren Mahy', 'Wesley Burt', 'Willian Murai', 'Yeong-Hao Han', 'Yohann Schepacz', 'Zoltan Boros', 'Zoltan Boros & Gabor Szikszai', 'rk post']
